module.exports = "At SBC Summit I discovered a skill my inner child strongly disapproves of: walking up to complete strangers and starting a conversation.\n\nThis has never come naturally to me. Add a goal — learn about the company, understand the product, ask about roles — and it usually becomes even harder.\n\nBut during the event I kept doing it: start with small talk, listen for what matters to the other person, find an intersection, then move toward the question I actually came with.\n\nAt some point a couple of people started joining me, and we went from booth to booth together.\n\nMy inner child was shouting: “We do not talk to strangers.”\n\nAdult me kept saying: “Hi. What are you working on?”\n\nThat was a useful reminder: networking is not an extrovert’s magic trick. It is a trainable sequence of small moves. I still feel the resistance. I am just getting better at acting before it wins.";
